Author: Diana Z <dzigterman@chromium.org>
Date:   Fri Nov 16 12:59:47 2018 -0700

    PD: Respect tTypeCSendSourceCap timing
    
    Currently, the pd_task will send source capability messages every time
    the task wakes while in PD_STATE_SRC_DISCOVERY.  This can cause the task
    to violate the required 100-200 ms gap between sending source
    capabilities during source advertisement, and in a worst case it will
    give up sending source cabilities well before it should.
    
    With this change, the task should send a source capability message
    almost exactly every 100ms while in PD_STATE_SRC_DISCOVERY.
    
    BRANCH=None
    BUG=b:117788783
    TEST=plugged hoho into bobba360 and phaser repeatedly with no hard
    resets during initial connection
    
    Change-Id: Id968921e0b0ea874bf7361849c22354804b5b9ca
    Signed-off-by: Diana Z <dzigterman@chromium.org>
    Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1340546
