Author: Scott Collyer <scollyer@google.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 16 16:36:33 2018 -0700

    ppc: syv682x: Make source disable dependent on VBUS presence
    
    The syv682x PPC does not provide independent disabling of the source
    and sink paths. Instead there is a single bit PWR_ENB, which when set,
    will disable both the source and sink paths.
    
    As part of USB PD initialization, pd_power_supply_reset(0) is called
    to ensure VBUS isn't being sourced. If the source path isn't currently
    active, then PWR_ENB bit should not be set as that will also disable
    the sink path which may be active in a dead battery start up case.
    
    This CL modifies the syv682x driver to only set PWR_ENB if the bit in
    flags is set to indicate that the VBUS was being sourced.
    
    BRANCH=none
    BUG=b:117657778
    TEST=Tested on DragonEgg. With no battery, connected external to port
    1 and verified that the system boots successfully. Previously, it
    would lose power.
    
