    flash-stm32h7: Invalidate D-cache after erase/write operations
    
    When erasing or writing to the flash, the core may still have
    some of the old data in cache. Among other things, this confuses
    flashrom when it tries to read back an erased block, as it thinks
    that the erase operation was unsuccessful.
    
    This, of course, will have some moderate performance impact when
    doing memory operations, but hopefully those are rare enough to
    not matter significantly.
    
    The I-cache does not have such issues, as we invalidate it on
    sysjump/boot, when it actually matters.
    
