    npcx: adc: only enable ADC during conversion for power consumption.
    
    For better power consumption in npcx series ec, this CL only turns on
    ADC module before starting conversion and turns it off after the
    conversion is done.
    
    If ec enters deep sleep when ADC conversion is ongoing, the conveting
    process is suspended until next time ec wakes up from the deep sleep.
    Considering the frequency of ADC's source clock is up to 15MHz, it's
    more efficient to forbid ec enter deep sleep when the conversion
    is proceeding. (Each conversion time of ADC channel is ~200us based on
    this condition.) Forbidding ec enter deep sleep should have no harm.
    
    BRANCH=none
